From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: ingenic: add the T41

The T41 pin controller is the PAT0/PAT1 block of the older parts: a mux
value of 0..3 per pin written through the pattern registers, no shadow
window, and a pull-up/pull-down bit per pin in separate registers at
0x110 and 0x120 rather than the shared pull-enable bit field the JZ4770
and X1000 use.

Register four banks 0x1000 apart (PA-PD, 128 pins), the pin groups and
functions from the vendor device tree (each vendor group is a bank, a pin
range and one function selector, which maps onto a group with a single
mux value), and the T41 bias path in ingenic_set_bias() and
ingenic_pinconf_get().

The version value sits between JZ4780 and X1000: the mux programming then
takes the direct PAT0/PAT1 path instead of X1000's shadow registers, and
the X1830 schmitt/slew pinconf options stay off.

Checked under QEMU: the SFC0 group (PA23-PA28, function 1) comes out as
PAT0 = 0x1f800000 and PAT1 = 0, which is the expected bitmap.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
